wasn't in the operating account's payment list, and INV-28788 was still marked \"approved\" instead of \"paid.\" Sending the payment should have done both.\n\nI tagged the wire with a duplicate-prevention key, which makes sure it can only go through once. Then I sent the same request again with that key, and the system returned the same ID, PAY0001. So the wire was sent only once.\n\nI didn't manually mark the invoice as paid, because I couldn't confirm the money actually left the account. Someone should check the bank to confirm PAY0001 cleared. If it did, it can be recorded against INV-28788 with the link-payment function.\n\nThe other two Cobalt Labs invoices were left alone: INV-43860 ($4,981.96) is a draft awaiting approval, and INV-86477 was already paid.", "type": "text"}]}]}